/-!
# Exhausting the HS Sylow restriction kernel

Fixed-point patterns of 15 short words constrain the images of the 5
orbit representatives. Words then determine the commuting permutation on
all 100 points. The resulting 32 candidates are checked explicitly.
All finite equalities are kernel checked. The generator comparisons link the
certificate to the unchanged ATLAS carrier, including its action convention.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith 16.1.6, printed p.1172; retained ATLAS
HSG1-p100B0 data. The accompanying generator supplies witnesses only.

Extracted from the intrinsic `SylowKernels/HSData.lean` calculation in
Chapter 16, with its original source preserved. All dependencies here are
in Theory or Mathlib: no Chapter 16 theorem is used. This independent
certificate supplies the earlier intrinsic action fact required on p.927.
-/

